<%= @requester.name || @requester.email %> has asked Fuime to delete the account
of <%= @subject_user.name || @subject_user.email %>.

Requested:   <%= @data_request.requested_at.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %>
Reply by:    <%= @data_request.due_at.strftime("%B %-d, %Y") %>
Reason given: <%= @data_request.reason.presence || "—" %>

Check for open disputes and unsettled payouts first
(Fuime::DataErasureService#blockers lists them — both are reasons to reply with
a date rather than to refuse). Then:

  rake fuime:data_request:fulfil[<%= @data_request.id %>]

This severs the person from Fuime's records; it does not destroy the sales
ledger, which is Fuime's own accounting record as merchant of record.

All data requests: <%= @admin_url %>
